# The sizzle-reel staging mission (dev-only).
#
# It does not play anything. A staging label spawns a scene, binds the cast the shot
# list names, and loads shots.amd; the capture harness then steps the shots one at a
# time so a still can be grabbed while the camera holds.

import maps/sz_stage.mast


# Every page - server and client - parks, in a SCHEDULED task.
#
# Two rules collide here and only this shape satisfies both:
#
#   * A GUI task that ENDS closes its page and blanks the screen - mast.runtime.log
#     says so in as many words ("has no tasks left, so its page is being closed").
#     A blank client is not something you can photograph.
#   * Top-level code from EVERY loaded file is combined into one shared main, so an
#     `await` at the top level blocks that main for everyone. Awaiting here stalls
#     the cosmos_devqueue mastlib's own top-level `task_schedule(...)` before it
#     ever runs, and the harness then waits out its timeout on a queue that was
#     never started.
#
# So: schedule the park and let main run on.
task_schedule(sz_park)


=== sz_park ===
    # One empty row, deliberately. `await gui()` with no build at all is a black
    # screen, but anything drawn would sit on top of the shot - what the camera
    # client shows is set by shot_apply, which switches it to the cinematic view.
    gui_blank()
    await gui()
